Limitations and Recommendations
Wide Confidence Intervals: Static CIs for ust10y suggest limited model sensitivity to new inputs. Consider recomputing CIs using rolling prediction variance.
Slope Change Threshold: ±0.01 threshold results in mostly unchanged. Lowering to ±0.005 may capture more dynamics.
Model Sensitivity: High reliance on slope_10y_2y_lag1 (98.43% importance) may limit forecast variability. Removing or scaling this feature could improve dynamics.
Alternative Models: ARIMA or LSTM models may better capture time series trends, especially for slope_10y_2y, given historical inaccuracies (Aug 2024–Jan 2025).
Date Range: Forecasts start April 29, 2025, due to code oversight. Adjusted to May 1, 2025, in this report.
